# .agentignore: paths the factory agent may never read, search, copy, send or write.
#
# Enforced by .claude/hooks/guard.py, a PreToolUse hook, for the Read, Edit, Write and
# Grep tools and for paths named in shell commands. Mirrored in .claude/settings.json
# deny rules as a second layer.
#
# Syntax is .gitignore's: a name with no slash matches anywhere, a leading "/" or a
# slash anchors to the repo root, "~/" is the home folder, "**" is any depth, a
# trailing "/" covers a folder, and "!" re-allows a path.
#
# The guard already protects common secrets: .env files, private keys, SSH, AWS,
# GitHub CLI and Claude credentials. See DEFAULT_SECRET_PATTERNS in guard.py.
# Add anything project-specific here. Only a human should edit this file; the guard
# stops the agent from changing it.

# Project secrets and local overrides
secrets/
*.secret
*.secrets.*
config/local.*
.envrc

# Infrastructure credentials
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
kubeconfig
*kubeconfig*.yaml

# Proxmox and Home Assistant (docs/security/least-privilege.md)
**/pve-*.token
**/proxmox*.token
**/proxmox*.env
secrets.yaml
ha-token*
.storage/auth*

# DeepSec findings stay out of the agent's hands, too: they describe live vulnerabilities.
.deepsec/findings/
.deepsec/.env.local
